implementationPlan.description:
TESTS FIRST (red) for the helper. Load test-driven-development.

New file moe-jetbrains/src/test/kotlin/com/moe/services/DaemonIdentityTest.kt (JUnit 4, headless, like its neighbours). It runs against a real com.sun.net.httpserver.HttpServer bound to 127.0.0.1:0, stopped in @After.

CLASSIFICATION RULE, identical to the proxy sibling task-86093c3e (amend-1) and the planner note comment-927340a6:
- Only HTTP 200 (healthy) or 503 (unhealthy) with a JSON-object body counts.
- projectPath must be a non-empty ABSOLUTE path: a drive letter, UNC (\\\\ or //) or POSIX (/). A relative path is Unknown, because the daemon reports its raw --project argument (packages/moe-daemon/src/index.ts ~:61).
- Then compare comparable forms: Same if equal, otherwise Foreign(servedPath). Everything else is Unknown.

Rows for DaemonIdentityProbe.probe(port, ownPath):
- Same, with own 'D:/proj' against the replies 'D:\\proj', 'd:/proj', 'D:/proj/' and '/mnt/d/proj'. All four are Same.
- Same: own '//wsl$/Ubuntu/home/u/p' against reply '/home/u/p', and '\\\\wsl.localhost\\Ubuntu\\home\\u\\p' against '/home/u/p'. A WSL-hosted daemon serving this project must never be Foreign.
- Foreign:
  - reply 'D:/other' -> Foreign('D:/other');
  - 503 {status:'unhealthy', projectPath:'D:/other'} -> Foreign;
  - 503 with this project -> Same.
- Unknown:
  - relative replies '.' and 'sub/p';
  - no projectPath;
  - projectPath 42 or '';
  - non-JSON;
  - a JSON array;
  - a body over 64 KiB;
  - statuses 426 and 500;
  - unreachable (a port from a stopped server);
  - timeout: a handler that sleeps past a 200 ms read timeout. The row must finish under 2 s.
- The probe never throws.

Also pure rows for comparableProjectPath and isAbsoluteAnyOs on the same spellings, plus '..' and '.' segments. Run `gradlew test --tests com.moe.services.DaemonIdentityTest` and confirm it is red, because the helper does not exist yet.

New file moe-jetbrains/src/main/kotlin/com/moe/services/DaemonIdentity.kt: a pure helper with no platform services.

- `sealed interface DaemonIdentity { object Same; data class Foreign(val projectPath: String); object Unknown }`.
- `object DaemonIdentityProbe` holds:
  - const MAX_HEALTH_BODY_BYTES = 64 * 1024;
  - `fun probe(port: Int, projectPath: String, connectTimeoutMs: Int = 500, readTimeoutMs: Int = 1000): DaemonIdentity`;
  - internal pure `classify(status: Int, body: String?, projectPath: String)`;
  - `comparableProjectPath(path: String): String`;
  - `isAbsoluteAnyOs(path: String): Boolean`.

probe:
- Open `URL("http://127.0.0.1:$port/health").openConnection(java.net.Proxy.NO_PROXY) as HttpURLConnection`. Use NO_PROXY so the IDE's HTTP proxy settings can never route a loopback probe.
- requestMethod GET, instanceFollowRedirects false, both timeouts set.
- Read inputStream for 200, or errorStream for 503, reading at most MAX+1 bytes; over the cap is Unknown.
- Parse with Gson (`JsonParser.parseString`) and require a JsonObject.
- Catch every Exception into Unknown, and call disconnect() in a finally.

comparableProjectPath, string-level and OS-independent, mirroring the proxy's comparableProjectPath (packages/moe-proxy/src/utils.ts ~:31):
- trim and turn backslashes into '/';
- map `//wsl$/<distro>/rest` and `//wsl.localhost/<distro>/rest` (case-insensitive) to `/rest`;
- collapse '.', '..', duplicate slashes and a trailing slash, keeping a leading '//' for other UNC paths;
- map `/mnt/<d>/rest` to `<d>:/rest`;
- lowercase drive-letter and UNC forms, and keep POSIX case.

The Same/Foreign rule must err toward Same or Unknown: a false Foreign deletes daemon.json and spawns a duplicate daemon. A header comment says this, and names the proxy twin.

Run DaemonIdentityTest until it is green.

implementationPlan.note:
QA issue 2 fixed in DaemonIdentity.kt. HttpURLConnection's responseCode reads status and headers under an inactivity-only timeout, so on JDK 17 (no HttpClient.shutdownNow) probe() now does an HTTP/1.0 GET over `Socket(Proxy.NO_PROXY).use { }` on the calling thread:
- connect to 127.0.0.1:<port> within connectTimeoutMs (at least 1);
- write `GET /health HTTP/1.0`, `Host: 127.0.0.1:<port>`, `Connection: close`;
- new private readReply: before each read, soTimeout = min(readTimeoutMs, time left to the deadline), at least 1 (never 0, which means infinite). It returns null at the deadline or past MAX_REPLY_BYTES (the 64 KiB body cap plus 8 KiB for the head), and EOF ends the reply;
- new private parseReply: the status line must match `HTTP/1.[01] ddd`, the head must end in CRLFCRLF, and the body must be within the 64 KiB cap, then the unchanged classify runs. Anything else is Unknown.
So connect, status, headers and body all end by connect + read. No thread is created, and `use` closes the socket on every path. A raw socket follows no redirect, and NO_PROXY bypasses every ProxySelector. classify, comparableProjectPath and isAbsoluteAnyOs are unchanged.
Protocol check against the LIVE moes daemon (Node), with the same request bytes: `HTTP/1.1 200 OK`, `Connection: close`, no Content-Length or chunking, and EOF 2 ms after a 364-byte body. With an HTTP/1.1 request, writeHead-then-end would chunk.
Test fix in DaemonIdentityTest: the 'unreachable' row now takes its port from a released ServerSocket. On JDK 21, a never-started HttpServer still LISTENS after stop(0), measured with a one-file java.exe check. The old row therefore connected and waited out the 1 s read timeout, the same 1.003 s on the old code in QA's XML, and never tested a refused connect. It now takes 11 ms.
GREEN, same focused command: exit 0, 18 tests, 0 failures/errors/skips, XML 09:53:30.6Z after the Windows start 09:53:28.3Z. The header trickle took 0.518 s, against 10087 ms before.

implementationPlan.description:
VERIFY ONCE, fresh, then ADVERSARIAL SELF-REVIEW.

Take the shared resource 'jetbrains-gradle' with moe.acquire_resource first. If it is busy, call moe.report_blocked with resourceId 'jetbrains-gradle'. Release it after the run. Then run, from WSL:

cmd.exe /d /c "set GRADLE_OPTS=-Xmx512m&& cd /d D:\projexts\moes\moe-jetbrains && .\gradlew.bat test --rerun"

It must exit 0. Its command, exit code and output tail are complete_task's evidence. Before citing it, confirm that DaemonIdentityTest, MoeProjectForeignDaemonTest and the unedited MoeProjectConnectionTest ran.

Mutants, on scratch copies, each turning the named rows red:
(i) compare raw strings: the Same spelling rows;
(ii) delete daemon.json unconditionally: F2;
(iii) treat Unknown as Foreign: U1 and the Unknown rows;
(iv) drop the connecting = false before scheduleReconnect: F1's reconnectFuture assertion.

Then load adversarial-self-review and check:
- a false Foreign: Windows vs WSL vs \\\\wsl$ spellings, case, trailing slash, a relative path;
- the probe on the EDT;
- a second client from a concurrent connect;
- a disposal during the probe;
- the IDE proxy (NO_PROXY);
- a slow or trickling /health (both timeouts plus the byte cap);
- the compare-then-delete window. It is best-effort: a new daemon writes a new startedAt.

A read-only `git status --short` must show only the four owned paths, and MoeDaemonSupervisor.kt untouched. Never revert, stash, `git add -A` or commit peer or pre-existing paths. Write the Serena handoff 'task-task-90664db1e08a45f7b63c1e0f44eeee09-handoff' for task-e7f4026a (the final verification row) and CQ-RF04 (task-de91373a, which edits MoeProjectService.kt next).
